addresses.comment:
**The writer of `CDiplomacyStatus +0x38 relation`, which the record had as inferred with no writer identified.** 0x4E65C0 to the two `ret 4`s at 0x4E662B and 0x4E6635 - one body, two arms of the same clamp - 8 int3 before 0x4E6640. The receiver is in **EDI** and the other country's tag in **ECX**, with the delta the one stack argument, so it carries no ordinary calling convention and the annotations are explicit (trap 11).

    fwd = this->diplomacy[other->id];          // CCountry +0xE28
    fwd->changed (+0x59) = 1;
    v = clamp(delta + fwd->relation (+0x38), [0x1710C38], [0x1710C34]);
    fwd->relation = v;
    rev = other->GetCountry()->diplomacy[this->id];   // CCountryTag::GetCountry, 0x402610
    rev->changed = 1;
    rev->relation = v;

So **relation is symmetric by construction** - the same clamped value is written to both directions, and the delta is applied to the forward side's current value only. The two clamp globals are `[0x1710C34] = 200000` and `[0x1710C38] = -200000`, i.e. **relation is thousandths on a -200.000..+200.000 scale** (trap 7), which is the range the game's own diplomacy screen shows. **Twenty-four call sites, not eighteen, and six are outside the diplomatic-action family** (corrected 2026-10-12): eighteen in the nine actions' slot 7, two in CFaction::AddCountry, one each in CLiberateCountryCommand::Execute, CCombat::Conclude, CRelationEffect::Execute and CReleaseVassalEffect::Execute. Most pass a diplomacy define (stored x1000); three pass one negated, and five pass a constant (+5, -30, +10, -20, +500). **It is also inlined, so it is not the only writer of +0x38**: the same add, clamp and both-ways store is in MakeVassal (0x4DA37D/0x4DA3B7, +500), CCreateVassalCommand::Execute (0x54C219/0x54C266, +500) and the monthly drift in CCountry::UpdateMonthly (0x4DCCF0/0x4DCD27). CRelationChange::Apply (rva 0x1F2CA0), CDiplomacyStatus::SetValue (rva 0x648160, a loaded save) and the new-game set at 0x4D7316 write one side only. The table of every change is section C of reversing/findings/FINDINGS-diplostate.md.
